  "method": "ninfer-serve startup capacity (public server_start event) followed by one concurrent request per lane with an 8-token budget, at every C1..12 (adaptive DFlash K7) and C1..16 (adaptive MTP K3), for both KV caches. Natural stop tokens stay enabled, so some requests ended early. Each startup waits for 5 s of idle device memory after the previous owner exits, and physical free VRAM (amdgpu counters) is sampled every 50 ms through startup and decode.",
  "notes": [
    "Allocated shared capacity, not an all-lane near-capacity qualification.",
    "C1/C2 (and NVFP4 C3) reach the C x max_context ceiling.",
    "Raw startup events, logs and responses remain local under the session scratch directory.",
    "Every cell keeps at least the 32-MiB default headroom physically free; the NVFP4 C4..8 driver-residency addend is included.",
    "Raw startup events, server logs and responses: profiles/upstream-sync/20261108/cap/final, with final2 remeasuring NVFP4 DFlash C3..9, NVFP4 MTP C4..8 and a default DFlash C8 control on the final build."
